WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.966
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:09.826
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.126 --> 00:00:17.736
Unit fourteen: Pronunciation, Stress and Intonation. Today you will stress the right syllable and use clear intonation.

4
00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:20.723
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:24.783
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:26.616
Syllable.

7
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:29.999
Syllable means a unit of sound in a word.

8
00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:32.362
Banana has three syllables.

9
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.486
Your turn. Say: Syllable.

10
00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:39.532
Syllable.

11
00:00:40.283 --> 00:00:41.250
Stress.

12
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.760
Stress means extra force on a syllable.

13
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.955
Stress the first syllable.

14
00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.121
Your turn. Say: Stress.

15
00:00:52.967 --> 00:00:54.049
Stress.

16
00:00:54.783 --> 00:00:55.866
Intonation.

17
00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.627
Intonation means the rise and fall of the voice.

18
00:01:00.217 --> 00:01:01.938
Use rising intonation.

19
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.435
Your turn. Say: Intonation.

20
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.278
Intonation.

21
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:10.762
Vowel.

22
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.388
Vowel means a, e, i, o or u sound.

23
00:01:14.983 --> 00:01:16.112
A is a vowel.

24
00:01:16.717 --> 00:01:19.415
Your turn. Say: Vowel.

25
00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:23.094
Vowel.

26
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.805
Consonant.

27
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:28.037
Consonant means a letter that is not a vowel.

28
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.069
B is a consonant.

29
00:01:30.683 --> 00:01:32.976
Your turn. Say: Consonant.

30
00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:36.800
Consonant.

31
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.423
Silent.

32
00:01:39.417 --> 00:01:41.230
Silent means not pronounced.

33
00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:43.271
K is silent in knife.

34
00:01:43.883 --> 00:01:46.245
Your turn. Say: Silent.

35
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.066
Silent.

36
00:01:50.817 --> 00:01:51.736
Rhythm.

37
00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.504
Rhythm means a pattern of strong and weak sounds.

38
00:01:56.117 --> 00:01:57.768
English has a clear rhythm.

39
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:01.140
Your turn. Say: Rhythm.

40
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:04.722
Rhythm.

41
00:02:05.483 --> 00:02:06.484
Accent.

42
00:02:07.483 --> 00:02:09.367
Accent means a way of speaking.

43
00:02:09.983 --> 00:02:11.518
She has a clear accent.

44
00:02:12.117 --> 00:02:14.966
Your turn. Say: Accent.

45
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:18.906
Accent.

46
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.910
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.504
Visal, how do I find word stress?

48
00:02:27.617 --> 00:02:42.311
Check the dictionary. Many two-syllable nouns are stressed on the first syllable, such as TAble, and many verbs on the second, such as reLAX. Words ending in -tion stress the syllable before it.

49
00:02:43.417 --> 00:02:44.929
What about intonation?

50
00:02:46.017 --> 00:03:00.883
Use falling intonation for statements and wh- questions, and rising intonation for yes/no questions. Rising voice also shows that a list is not finished.

51
00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:03.530
What about silent letters?

52
00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:15.512
Some letters are not pronounced, such as k in knife, b in doubt and w in write. Learn them in words, and practise with a recording of your own voice.

53
00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.399
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.167
Grammar focus: stress, intonation and sounds.

55
00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:23.561
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.670
Do you like tea? ↗

57
00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:29.899
Where do you live? ↘

58
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:38.382
Stress the right syllable, use falling intonation for statements and wh- questions, and rising intonation for yes/no questions.

59
00:03:39.117 --> 00:03:42.593
Be careful! Don't say: I stress the wrong syllable.

60
00:03:44.533 --> 00:03:47.044
Say: I check the stress in a dictionary.

61
00:03:47.344 --> 00:03:48.484
Check stress.

62
00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:52.185
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.419
Speaking Clearly.

64
00:03:54.719 --> 00:03:57.671
Rotha practises English pronunciation every day.

65
00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:01.549
She checks the stress of new words in a dictionary.

66
00:04:02.533 --> 00:04:05.671
She uses rising intonation for yes/no questions.

67
00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:09.235
She records her voice and listens again.

68
00:04:10.233 --> 00:04:12.465
Her speaking is clearer every week.

69
00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:17.580
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:18.417 --> 00:04:20.428
A syllable is a unit of blank.

71
00:04:20.728 --> 00:04:24.404
A, spelling. B, number. C, sound.

72
00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.815
The answer is C: sound.

73
00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.426
Yes/no questions use blank intonation.

74
00:04:33.726 --> 00:04:37.077
A, rising. B, falling. C, no.

75
00:04:40.633 --> 00:04:42.436
The answer is A: rising.

76
00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.107
The k in knife is blank.

77
00:04:45.407 --> 00:04:48.306
A, a vowel. B, silent. C, loud.

78
00:04:51.867 --> 00:04:53.878
The answer is B: silent.

79
00:04:55.017 --> 00:04:58.003
Wh- questions often use blank intonation.

80
00:04:58.303 --> 00:05:01.724
A, rising. B, flat. C, falling.

81
00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:07.197
The answer is C: falling.

82
00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.291
How does Rotha check stress?

83
00:05:10.591 --> 00:05:14.663
A, a dictionary. B, a map. C, a calendar.

84
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.211
The answer is A: a dictionary.

85
00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.319
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:25.183 --> 00:05:27.183
How do you practise pronunciation?

87
00:05:35.983 --> 00:05:37.530
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:49.483
I check word stress in a dictionary and I repeat new words aloud. I record my voice and listen to my mistakes. I also copy the intonation of my teacher.

89
00:05:49.783 --> 00:05:51.562
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:57.517
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and stress, intonation and sounds.

91
00:05:57.817 --> 00:06:02.977
Today's value is self-discipline. Control your habits, so your habits do not control you.

92
00:06:03.277 --> 00:06:05.872
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:06.172 --> 00:06:08.975
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

